<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Linear SCM experiment</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the experiment underlying Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we sampled 3,000 linear SCMs with 9 variables (including the target). To this end, we applied Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="In C.2 Linear SCM experiment ‣ Appendix C Experimental details and additional results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=9</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.8</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain a random adjacency matrix <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and then used i.i.d. random variables <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{9}\sim\mathrm{Laplace}(0;0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mn>9</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Laplace</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1},U_{2},\ldots,U_{9}\sim\mathrm{Laplace}(0;0.1)</annotation></semantics></math> (Laplace distribution with mean <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and scale <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>) to define the linear SCM</p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{V}=A\mathbf{V}+\mathbf{U}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{V}=A\mathbf{V}+\mathbf{U}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{9}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the variables of the SCM and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}=(U_{i})_{1\leq i\leq 9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}=(U_{i})_{1\leq i\leq 9}</annotation></semantics></math> collects the noise variables. For each noise instance <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, equation (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In C.2 Linear SCM experiment ‣ Appendix C Experimental details and additional results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) was solved for <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}=(I-A)^{-1}\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}=(I-A)^{-1}\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Sample adjacency matrix of a linear SCM</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Number of variables <math id="algorithm2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, edge probability <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>adjacency matrix <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"># </span><span id="algorithm2.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Create random binary matrix </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">Sample i.i.d. <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{i,j}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{i,j}\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{1\leq i,j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{1\leq i,j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">Create <math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A\leftarrow[U_{i,j}&lt;p]_{1\leq i,j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\leftarrow[U_{i,j}&lt;p]_{1\leq i,j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"># </span><span id="algorithm2.4.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Turn into binary adjacency matrix </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">For all <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq j</annotation></semantics></math> set <math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline">Draw a random <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-permutation <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline">Permute rows and columns of <math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter"># </span><span id="algorithm2.4.10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Fill with random floats </span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline">Sample i.i.d. <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{ij}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{1\leq i,j\leq n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{1\leq i,j\leq n}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">Replace <math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}\leftarrow A_{ij}\cdot\alpha_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}\leftarrow A_{ij}\cdot\alpha_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">From each SCM constructed as above, we sampled <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\cdot 10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\cdot 10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> samples of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math>. Target and features are constructed from <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐕</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}</annotation></semantics></math> via the assignment:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{1}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{1}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{i+1}\mbox{ for all }1\leq i\leq 8." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{i+1}\mbox{ for all }1\leq i\leq 8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The analysis behind Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> then focuses on the relation between <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y,X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y,X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computation of <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}},\,b_{X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>do</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}},\,b_{X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\emptyset}(X_{1}),I_{X_{2}}(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\emptyset}(X_{1}),I_{X_{2}}(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}(X_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mi>do</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}(X_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> only differ from <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1}],\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1},X_{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1}],\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1},X_{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>do</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Y|X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})]</annotation></semantics></math> via <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>-independent terms we used the latter to obtain
<math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}},\,b_{X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>do</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}},\,b_{X_{1},\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the observational quantities <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{X_{1}},\,b_{X_{1}|X_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> we fitted linear univariate and bivariate models with least-squares loss on the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\cdot 10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\cdot 10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> samples described above. For the causal quantity <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{X_{1}|\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>do</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{X_{1}|\mathrm{do}(X_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math>, we made a stochastic intervention on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E19" title="In C.2 Linear SCM experiment ‣ Appendix C Experimental details and additional results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) as described in Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In Using the SCM. ‣ 3.2 Estimation ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and then conducted another least-squares fit of a bivariate linear model on <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\cdot 10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\cdot 10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> samples of the modified model. We used least-squares fitting, instead of maximum likelihood fitting, due to the optimality of conditional expectation under the <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L2</annotation></semantics></math>-norm, cf. Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma B.1 (Conditional expectation as optimally trained model). ‣ B.1 Conditional expectation as optimal model ‣ Appendix B Further theoretical aspects ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> above.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Collider impact.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The “Collider impact” indicated in the colorbar of Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4 Experimental results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is measured via a heuristic quantity that is defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mbox{Collider impact}=\frac{|CP_{X_{2}}|}{|CP_{X_{2}}|+|UP_{X_{2}}|}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Collider impact</mtext><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mbox{Collider impact}=\frac{|CP_{X_{2}}|}{|CP_{X_{2}}|+|UP_{X_{2}}|}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle CP_{X_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle CP_{X_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\mbox{\small$X_{1},Y$ paths containing $X_{2}$ as the only collider}}\prod A_{ij}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext mathsize="1.280em"> paths containing </mtext><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mtext mathsize="1.280em"> as the only collider</mtext></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\mbox{\small$X_{1},Y$ paths containing $X_{2}$ as the only collider}}\prod A_{ij}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle UP_{X_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle UP_{X_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\mbox{\small unblocked $X_{1},Y$ path containing $X_{2}$}}\prod A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mtext mathsize="1.280em">unblocked </mtext><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Y</mi></mrow><mtext mathsize="1.280em"> path containing </mtext><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">X</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\mbox{\small unblocked $X_{1},Y$ path containing $X_{2}$}}\prod A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">denote the sum of products of entries of the adjacency matrix along the paths indicated under the summation symbols. In particular, if all paths between <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> that run through <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and are either unblocked or contain <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as the only collider, all fall in the second category, the “Collider impact” will be 1. If they are all unblocked, “Collider Impact” will be 0. Object (<a href="#A3.E22" title="In Collider impact. ‣ C.2 Linear SCM experiment ‣ Appendix C Experimental details and additional results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>) is (loosely) motivated by Wright’s path tracing rules <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wright, 1934</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pearl, 2013</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the analysis of paths between <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, we used the <span id="A3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">NetworkX</span> package from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hagberg et al. [2007]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Diabetes and BMI example</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The precise SCM for the nonlinear example outlined in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental results ‣ cc-Shapley: Measuring Multivariate Feature Importance Needs Causal Context" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> was entirely hand-crafted and is given by</p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{aligned} B&amp;=U_{B},\,U_{B}\sim\mathcal{N}(25;5)\\
Y&amp;\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(\sigma(-2+0.1\cdot(B-25)))\\
H&amp;=5+10\cdot Y+0.01\cdot B^{2}+U_{H},\,U_{H}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;1)\\
G&amp;=90+20\cdot Y+30\cdot\sigma(-0.5\cdot(H-5))+B+U_{G},\,U_{G}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;5)\;,\end{aligned}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>B</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>Y</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Bernoulli</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>H</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mi>G</mi></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>U</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{aligned} B&amp;=U_{B},\,U_{B}\sim\mathcal{N}(25;5)\\
Y&amp;\sim\mathrm{Bernoulli}(\sigma(-2+0.1\cdot(B-25)))\\
H&amp;=5+10\cdot Y+0.01\cdot B^{2}+U_{H},\,U_{H}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;1)\\
G&amp;=90+20\cdot Y+30\cdot\sigma(-0.5\cdot(H-5))+B+U_{G},\,U_{G}\sim\mathcal{N}(0;5)\;,\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sigmoid function.</p>
</div>
